figma-bridge-mcp
================

This product includes third-party material.


engine/ — derived from figma-ds-cli
-----------------------------------

The `engine/` directory began in July 2026 as a vendored copy of:

    figma-ds-cli (a.k.a. "figma-cli")
    Version:  2.1.0
    Author:   Sil Bormüller (Into Design Systems)
    Source:   https://github.com/silships/figma-cli
    License:  MIT — retained in full at engine/LICENSE

It has since diverged, and is maintained as part of this project under its
own name (`figma-bridge-engine`) and its own version. Of the files vendored
at 2.1.0, four are still byte-identical: `code-import/css.js`,
`code-import/w3c-tokens.js`, `lib/design-md-locate.js`, `lib/motion-core.js`.
Everything else was rewritten, replaced, or removed. No byte-level parity
with upstream is maintained, and no upstream re-sync is planned.

Substantive changes relative to 2.1.0:

  removed   the Chrome DevTools Protocol transport and the binary-patching
            installer ("Yolo mode") — roughly 5,600 lines, along with the
            `figma-use` shell round-trip and the voice-plugin command group
  removed   every command not reachable through the MCP allowlist
  added     a mutual challenge-response handshake on the plugin WebSocket,
            so the access key never crosses the wire
  added     multi-file targeting, structural history snapshots and diffs,
            two-way token sync with a lockfile, FigJam authoring, Storybook
            mapping, and a design-to-code stack (extract / spec / code-spec /
            assets / verify-build)
  replaced  the JSX-to-plugin-code compiler, which now lives in
            `lib/jsx-render.js` and carries no transport of its own

Roughly 21,500 lines in `engine/` today; the majority is original to this
project. The upstream copyright and license notice above is retained for the
parts that are not, as MIT requires.


